  "description": "Positive/negative fixtures of the macOS catalog rules (wave 1), in the shape of a tested-registry entry's `fixtures`. Each string is `<base>:<relative path>`; base is home (CM_RESOLVE_HOME), temp (CM_RESOLVE_TEMP), downloads (CM_RESOLVE_DOWNLOADS) or volume (a selected volume root); a trailing `/` makes a directory. Every fixture is written 30 days old except those in `fresh`. With the overrides pointing at the fixture tree, a rule's candidates must be exactly its positive fixtures; `expect: permission_required` marks a privacy-protected (TCC) location that the resolver reports instead of reading. Fixtures are not registry evidence: no rule here is registered and every rule stays experimental until it is tested on a real Mac.",
